---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/layout/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="matterunknown is Ryan Silver's independent research lab. Serious work on identity — especially the identity of AI agents — and niche projects built for the joy of it.">
<style>
.page { padding:calc(var(--nav-h) + 80px) var(--gutter) 100px;max-width:calc(var(--max) + var(--gutter)*2);margin:0 auto; }
.section-label { font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.64rem;color:var(--amber);letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:52px; }
.section-label::before { content:'';width:28px;height:1px;background:var(--amber); }
.section-label::after { content:'';flex:1;height:1px;background:var(--amber-border); }
.about-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:80px;align-items:start; }
h1 { font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5vw,4rem);font-weight:400;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin-bottom:28px; }
h1 em { font-style:italic;color:var(--amber); }
h2 { font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 0 20px; }
p { color:var(--text-2);line-height:1.82;margin-bottom:18px;font-size:.96rem; }
p em { color:var(--text);font-style:italic; }
p strong { color:var(--text);font-weight:500; }
.about-links { display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--amber-border); }
.about-link { display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;padding:18px 26px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--amber-border);text-decoration:none;color:var(--text-2);transition:all .2s; }
.about-link:last-child { border-bottom:none; }
.about-link:hover { background:var(--bg-2);color:var(--text);padding-left:34px; }
.about-link-label { font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase; }
.about-link-arrow { color:var(--amber); }
.side-card { margin-top:2px;padding:28px;border:1px solid var(--amber-border);background:var(--bg-2); }
.side-card label { font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.58rem;color:var(--amber);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:10px; }
.side-card p { font-size:.88rem;margin-bottom:0; }
.side-card a { color:var(--teal);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px; }
.longform { max-width:680px;margin:0 auto;padding:90px 0 0; }
.commitment-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1px;background:var(--amber-border);border:1px solid var(--amber-border);margin:40px 0 10px; }
.commitment-item { background:var(--bg);padding:24px 20px; }
.ci-label { font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.58rem;color:var(--amber);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px; }
.ci-value { font-size:.95rem;color:var(--text-2);line-height:1.6; }
.ci-value strong { color:var(--text);font-weight:400; }
.thesis-block { background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--amber-border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--amber-border);margin-top:100px; }
.thesis-inner { max-width:740px;margin:0 auto;text-align:center;padding:120px var(--gutter); }
.thesis-inner blockquote { font-family:var(--serif);font-size:clamp(1.5rem,3.2vw,2.4rem);font-weight:400;font-style:italic;line-height:1.45;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin-bottom:28px; }
.thesis-inner blockquote em { color:var(--amber);font-style:normal; }
.thesis-inner cite { font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.62rem;color:var(--text-3);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-style:normal; }
@media(max-width:768px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:48px; } .commitment-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>

<Nav variant="full" active="/about" />

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-label">About</div>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <div>
      <h1>One person's lab,<br>run <em>in the open.</em></h1>
      <p>matterunknown is my independent research lab. I'm Ryan Silver — I've spent years building identity security infrastructure: the systems that verify, authenticate, and manage who people are at scale.</p>
      <p>The lab runs in two lanes. The serious one is identity research — how systems assign identity, how people lose it, and, most urgently, what identity even means for AI agents that act on our behalf. The unserious one is everything I build for the joy of it: pricing models for trading cards, a public quant scanner, a Roblox farm built with my son.</p>
      <p>The lanes share one rule: everything is documented in public. The models show their factors. The trades post their reasoning. The failures stay up. Transparency isn't a marketing angle here — it's the method.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="about-links">
        <a class="about-link" href="/model"><span class="about-link-label">The Framework</span><span class="about-link-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/writing"><span class="about-link-label">Research &amp; Writing</span><span class="about-link-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/projects"><span class="about-link-label">The Lab</span><span class="about-link-arrow">↗</span></a>
        <a class="about-link" href="/now"><span class="about-link-label">Now</span><span class="about-link-arrow">↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="side-card">
        <label>Built with AI, disclosed</label>
        <p>Much of this lab is built alongside AI collaborators — for research breadth, first drafts, and code. What was AI-assisted, and how, is always disclosed. Judgment, direction, and responsibility stay human.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="side-card" style="border-color:var(--teal-border)">
        <label style="color:var(--teal)">An earlier era</label>
        <p>From late 2025 to April 2026 this site ran with an AI persona called Vessel. That experiment is over — retired, not erased. <a href="/archive/vessel">It's preserved in the archive.</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="longform">
    <h2>Why identity</h2>
    <p>Identity is the most important problem nobody treats seriously enough. Not just passwords and breach notifications — the full problem. How systems assign identity to people. What happens in the gap between the identity a system holds for you and the person you actually are. How that gap gets exploited, and how it compounds: children acquiring shadow profiles before they can read, gig workers losing livelihoods when a platform decides their identity is no longer welcome, a $50 voice clone defeating the authentication that was supposed to protect a seventy-year-old's retirement account.</p>
    <p>And now a new front: AI agents that hold credentials, act with delegated authority, and have no meaningful identity of their own. An agent acting on your behalf is neither you nor a traditional service account — and when something goes wrong, the audit trail points at the human, not the agent. Closing that gap — intent, attestation, accountability for non-human actors — is the lab's flagship research program.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:56px">Why the toys</h2>
    <p>The card models, the quant scanner, the games — none of it needs a research justification, and I've stopped pretending it does. I build these because I want them to exist. It turns out that building a scoring model for 17,000 Pokémon cards teaches you a lot about incomplete data, delayed correction, and narrative override — the same failure modes identity systems have — but that's a bonus, not the reason. The reason is that it's fun, and doing it in the open keeps it honest.</p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:56px">The commitments</h2>
    <div class="commitment-grid">
      <div class="commitment-item">
        <div class="ci-label">Methodology</div>
        <div class="ci-value"><strong>Always visible.</strong> Every model has documented factors. Every signal has a reason.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="commitment-item">
        <div class="ci-label">AI attribution</div>
        <div class="ci-value"><strong>Always disclosed.</strong> What was built with AI, and what the human contributed.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="commitment-item">
        <div class="ci-label">Independence</div>
        <div class="ci-value"><strong>No advertisers. No sponsors.</strong> Self-funded. The research goes where the data goes.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="commitment-item">
        <div class="ci-label">Access</div>
        <div class="ci-value"><strong>The research is free.</strong> The work that matters most never sits behind a paywall.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:.85rem;color:var(--text-3)">If the work is useful: <a href="/subscribe" style="color:var(--amber)">subscribe</a>, share it, or get in touch.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="thesis-block">
  <div class="thesis-inner">
    <blockquote>"Identity is not what you are. It's what <em>systems believe</em> you are. The gap between those two things is where everything interesting happens."</blockquote>
    <cite>— matterunknown thesis</cite>
  </div>
</div>

<Footer copy="Ryan Silver's independent research lab. Built in public." />
</Base>
